,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.169151564,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.169882871,"data":"    build / total = 23.1% of the warm call\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.170592379,"data":"    GPU time      = ~109 ms, i.e. 0.56% of the warm call\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.171250827,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.172016155,"data":"    DECOMPOSITION of the 19.5 s warm call:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.172712116,"data":"        4.51 s   Python constructing UOps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.173409824,"data":"       14.88 s   TinyGrad's SCHEDULER (rewrite passes)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.17411271,"data":"        0.11 s   GPU execution (measured separately in perf_kda.py)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.174840362,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.175585977,"data":"    So it is NOT '99% Python'. It is mostly SCHEDULER.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.176309819,"data":"    The kernels ARE compiled once -- COLD is 49.5 s and WARM does not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.177060682,"data":"    recompile -- but tinygrad re-runs every rewrite pass on every\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.177803527,"data":"    realize(), because there is no separation between 'compile' and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.178492011,"data":"    'execute' in the API. A replay path that cached the SCHEDULED\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.179182343,"data":"    PROGRAM LIST, not just the compiled kernels, would bring the per-call\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.179923005,"data":"    cost down to the 109 ms of GPU time.\n"}
