,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.280174626,"data":"      so even a PERFECTLY fused KDA is still 2.1x below the H100 ridge point (295).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.28112715,"data":"      The gate + cumsum alone (steps 0,1) are 1280 MB = 52% of the traffic and 0 of the FLOPs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.281948687,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.282971106,"data":"    --- the traps (what a naive tensorised port would materialise) ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.283561185,"data":"    h, per-chunk states [B,NT,HV,K,V]      256.0 MB   (0.27 GB)  \u003c- only avoidable by fusing the scan\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.284263846,"data":"    full score matrix  [B,H,T,T]           4096.0 MB   (4.29 GB)  \u003c- softmax-attention shape; KDA must NOT do this\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.284987573,"data":"      per head: 32.0 MB, i.e. O(T^2).  A compiler that fuses the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.28570436,"data":"      chunk loop into one graph never has to build it -- but it also\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2744.286358114,"data":"      cannot parallelise the loop, which is the actual difficulty.\n"}
