,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2746.640283523,"data":"--- divide_precision: /usr/bin/python3 probes/divide_precision.py  (cwd=., timeout=900s) ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.577807249,"data":"    ==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.578670611,"data":"    Is TinyGrad's float32 `/` correctly rounded?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.579368135,"data":"    ==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.580092601,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.580823699,"data":"    1. a / a, which must be exactly 1.0 for every finite nonzero a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.581464497,"data":"       CPU   :       0 / 200,000 wrong  ( 0.00%)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.582144951,"data":"       CUDA  :  30,748 / 200,000 wrong  (15.37%)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.582863588,"data":"       CPU gives 1.0 everywhere. There is no 'approximation with its own\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.583497135,"data":"       validity condition' under which a/a != 1, so the failing backends\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.584164554,"data":"       are not implementing an allowed variant -- they are off by one ulp.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.584874648,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.585552846,"data":"    2. a / b against correctly rounded, per backend\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.586199158,"data":"       CUDA   :  54,270 wrong (27.13%)   == a*rcp(b) bit for bit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.586940193,"data":"       PYTHON :  54,270 wrong (27.13%)   == a*rcp(b) bit for bit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.587645425,"data":"       CPU    :       0 wrong ( 0.00%)   differs from rcp*mul\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.588326284,"data":"       CL     :  59,529 wrong (29.76%)   differs from rcp*mul\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.58902801,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.589718704,"data":"    3. the generated CUDA source for a single division\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.590389809,"data":"        *((float4*)((data0_64+alu0))) = make_float4((val0.x*(1/val1.x)),(val0.y*(1/val1.y)),(val0.z*(1/val1.z)),(val0.w*(1/val1.w)));\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.591088284,"data":"       =\u003e tinygrad's renderer emits `a*(1/b)`, not `a/b`. The backend then\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.591792587,"data":"          contracts the `1/b` into an approximate reciprocal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.592469111,"data":"    \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.593122573,"data":"    4. is the rewrite controllable?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.593826507,"data":"       Ops.RECIPROCAL exists and PTX renders it as `rcp.approx.f32` --\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.594486203,"data":"       an explicitly approximate op. But `/` does not go through it; the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.595144085,"data":"       cstyle renderer does the a*(1/b) rewrite unconditionally, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.595856792,"data":"       there is no flag for it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.596482816,"data":"  [ok     ] divide_precision      48.9s  the a*(1/b) rewrite\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.597133578,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":2795.597864049,"data":"--- gather_floor: /usr/bin/python3 probes/gather_floor.py  (cwd=., timeout=900s) ---\n"}
